# heighttoshadow

- Label: Height to Shadow
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 33 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttoshadow.html
- Summary (EN): Creates approximate shadows from a height field by placing a virtual light source and testing how much each pixel's neighbors block it. Intended for shading and texture synthesis.
- Résumé (FR) : Crée des ombres approximatives à partir d'un champ de hauteur, avec une lumière virtuelle de type disque, sphère ou directionnelle.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the original height layer used to calculate shadows"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Space", "meaning": "Local or World space for interpreting light position, direction and normal"}, {"name": "Height Map Scale", "meaning": "scales height values before occlusion is computed"}, {"name": "Step Scale", "meaning": "spacing of steps along each ray; larger cooks faster but may miss thin features"}, {"name": "Type", "meaning": "light profile: Disk, Sphere or Directional"}, {"name": "Radius / Angular Size", "meaning": "radius for Disk and Sphere; angular size in degrees for Directional"}, {"name": "Use / Light Normal", "meaning": "how Disk and Sphere positions are defined, and the Disk normal direction"}, {"name": "Single Sided", "meaning": "for Disk lights, ignores light from the back side"}]

- Caveats: ["The shadows are approximate, and thin features can be missed at higher Step Scale values."]

